Description: minimalist GTK 4 web browser with an original engine
 Northstar Web Browser is a web browser written from scratch
 in C, with a GTK 4 user interface and a libcurl network stack. It is built
 to be small, secure, and readable by a single person end to end.
 .
  * An original HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript engine — not a fork of
    Gecko, WebKit, or Blink.
  * No JIT, which keeps the JavaScript attack surface small.
  * Confined by a Landlock file-system allow-list and a seccomp
    system-call filter on Linux.
  * Plays MP3, Ogg, MPEG-1, and MP4 or WebM video (AV1, VP9) in
    process, without plugins.
  * No telemetry: it does not phone home and does not track the user.
